# Windows-only project (Windows PowerShell 5.1 on the customer stepping stone).
# The repository stores LF; every working tree gets CRLF. Spelling eol=crlf here makes that
# independent of each machine's core.autocrlf, which is a Git-for-Windows installer default
# rather than a project decision. text=auto still lets Git leave detected binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=crlf
